// STL Four Components

// 1- Itterators: They are used to traverse through the elements of a container. They provide a way to access the elements of a container without exposing the underlying structure of the container. They are similar to pointers and can be used to perform various operations on the elements of a container.

// 2- Functors: They are objects that can be called as if they were functions. They are used to define custom behavior for algorithms and can be used to create custom data structures. They are also known as function objects and can be used to create custom predicates for algorithms.

// 3- Algorithms: They are a set of instructions that can be used to perform various operations on the elements of a container. They are designed to work with iterators and can be used to perform various operations such as sorting, searching, and manipulating the elements of a container.

// 4- Containers: They are data structures that can hold a collection of elements. They provide various functions to manipulate the elements and can be used to store and manage data efficiently. Some common containers in STL include vector, list, deque, set, map, etc.